.el .ds Aq '
.TH ag-agent 1  "agent 0.3.0-beta.1" 
.SH NAME
ag\-agent \- Agent identities and runs
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBag agent\fR [\fB\-C\fR|\fB\-\-repo\fR] [\fB\-\-as\fR] [\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-\-color\fR] [\fB\-q\fR|\fB\-\-quiet\fR] [\fB\-v\fR|\fB\-\-verbose\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fB\-V\fR|\fB\-\-version\fR] <\fIsubcommands\fR>
.SH DESCRIPTION
Agent identities and runs
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-C\fR, \fB\-\-repo\fR \fI<DIR>\fR
Operate on the repository at this path (default: discovered from the current directory)
.TP
\fB\-\-as\fR \fI<IDENTITY>\fR
Act as this identity (`user:alice`, `agent:bot#run_…`, `service:ci`). Also: AG_IDENTITY
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Machine\-readable JSON output
.TP
\fB\-\-color\fR \fI<WHEN>\fR
Colour the output: auto (a terminal, unless NO_COLOR is set), always or never
.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-quiet\fR
Print only what was asked for: no confirmations or hints. Errors and refusals are still shown
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
Explain what is happening on standard error: repository, identity, remote, timing
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Print version
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
ag\-agent\-register(1)
Register an agent and create its signing key
.TP
ag\-agent\-list(1)
List agents
.TP
ag\-agent\-start(1)
Start a run. Prints the identity the agent must use (`agent:name#run_…`)
.TP
ag\-agent\-finish(1)
Finish a run and release its leases
.TP
ag\-agent\-heartbeat(1)
Heartbeat a running run
.TP
ag\-agent\-runs(1)
List runs, newest first
.TP
ag\-agent\-reap(1)
Abandon runs with no recent heartbeat and release their leases
.TP
ag\-agent\-disable(1)
Stop an agent from starting new runs
.TP
ag\-agent\-enable(1)
Allow a disabled agent to run again
.SH VERSION
v0.3.0\-beta.1
